% Plutus / RIVF'26 references
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Extracted from docs/reference/literature-review.md, section 6 "Sources"
% (the "Engine source and documentation" and "Literature" tables). Identifiers
% (arXiv / SSRN / NBER / DOI) are used exactly as the review gives them.
%
% Convention: an entry carrying `note = {... unverified ...}` is one the review
% did not resolve to a full, checkable citation (missing author/title/venue/year
% or a gazette-level primary source). Bibliographic detail is never invented to
% fill those gaps -- the note says so instead. Software projects that the review
% cites through many per-file evidence keys (L-*, N-*, RQ-*, ...) are collapsed
% to one entry per project.
%
% Software entries deliberately omit a publication `year`: the review cites a
% moving branch/version (e.g. "verified at branch master"), not a dated release,
% and a year is not invented for one. Under biblatex/biber this raises a benign
% "missing date/year" datamodel warning; under classic bibtex it is silent. The
% file parses in both.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

